// The moves of `arena_duelist_long`, the versus stage's reach fighter (Long Guard).
// The stage loads this file through its content pack (`assets/pack.ron`); edit it here.
//
// ONE GRAMMAR, TWO SETS OF NUMBERS. Both duelists answer the same four buttons
// with the same four moves: a jab (the fast poke you press when unsure), a
// grounded forward smash (the committed hit: slow enough to punish, heavy enough
// to risk; it decides how the fighter FEELS), an up tilt and a grounded down
// tilt. `arena_duelist_close.ron` is the same table with the other fighter's numbers.
// This fighter: jab 2, smash 9, reach 46 px, smash windup 0.26 s. The smash reaches 1.35 x the reach, the up tilt
// 0.8 x and the down tilt 0.9 x.
//
// A grounded-only move is SKIPPED for an airborne body rather than refused, so
// the directional chain falls through to the plain `attack`: an airborne
// fighter can still press the button. No move costs anything (nothing in the
// duel arena fills a meter) and none is a recovery (the arena authors no up-B).
